# Toyota Corolla E100 five-door liftback, 1992-1997.
#
# The seventh-generation Corolla. UK launch 7 August 1992; replaced when the
# E110 went on sale on 23 June 1997. A 1.6 Executive Liftback cost £13,210 in
# October 1992 according to a period road test, which is the only price found.
# https://mag.toyota.co.uk/toyota-corolla-generations-1992-1997/
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/pdf/Corolla-Timeline.pdf
#
# Dimensions 4.095 x 1.685 x 1.375 m, wheelbase 2.465 m. Source: English
# Wikipedia, "Toyota Corolla (E100)" infobox: wheelbase 2,465 mm; hatchback
# length 4,095 mm, sedan/coupe 4,275 mm and wagon/van 4,260 mm; width 1,685 mm;
# height 1,375 mm for sedan and hatchback. The hatchback figures apply, and the
# five-door liftback body is the one modelled. Body length 4.095 m before trim;
# mirrors extend beyond.
#
# Shape reference: the pack mixes a silver three-door, a blue five-door liftback
# and a further car. Image 1 supplied the roof line, arches and wheel positions
# but its three-door door cuts were not copied; images 2 and 3 supplied the
# front, the five-door divisions and the sloped hatch glass with its short
# painted lip and near-vertical rear panel. No boot is modelled. No true side
# elevation exists, so the wheel centres were fixed by the published 60.2 per
# cent wheelbase-to-length ratio.
#
# Colours: no Toyota GB brochure or price list for the 1992-1997 Corolla was
# found, and no British colour list exists in any other source consulted. The
# objects therefore carry plain colour names rather than invented marketing
# names: silver, white, black and red. Weights silver 3, white 3, red 2,
# black 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 175 km/h, between the 1.3-litre and 1.6-litre cars' quoted maxima.
# Comfort 80/450, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 80: a quiet, well-finished small
# family car for its year, a step above the superminis. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: August 1992 intro, retires staggered 2005-2008 on a
# thirteen- to sixteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-corolla-e100.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-corolla-e100.dae (66 objects). References:
# citycars/references/toyota-corolla-e100/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nose and tail are boxier than the photographs and
# the clear upper bands of the tail lamps are subdued. The top view and raised
# turn confirm a continuous painted roof. At 128 px the rounded three-box
# profile with its sloped hatch reads as the seventh-generation Corolla.

obj=citycar
name=ToyotaCorollaE100(Silver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1992
intro_month=8
retire_year=2008
retire_month=6
speed=175
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=80
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=450

Image[E]=./images/toyota-corolla-e100-silver_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/toyota-corolla-e100-silver_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/toyota-corolla-e100-silver_S.0.0,0,0
Image[SW]=./images/toyota-corolla-e100-silver_SW.0.0,-8,10
Image[W]=./images/toyota-corolla-e100-silver_W.0.0,4,5
Image[NW]=./images/toyota-corolla-e100-silver_NW.0.0,12,10
